        "summary": "Five identical type 222 enemies (hp 5, contact damage 1) sit in a tight cluster near (320,280) with rock cells at 51/53/81/83 bracketing them, so the clean firing corridor is the y=280 lane the player already occupies at (560,280). Default profile holds that lane: threat_first targeting locks the nearest body (3258758135:4 at 200 px, the only one inside the 195 px effective range), keep_range at 0.45-0.8 of range (~88-156 px) steps west just far enough to bring the cluster into range while staying outside contact, predictive aim with an 8-tick lead covers the nonzero v1 (0,40) vector these otherwise stationary bodies carry, and max_clearance evasion plus keep_routes escape preserve the open eastern retreat rather than committing into the rock pocket. Two normal-tear hits at 3.5 damage kill each 5 hp enemy, so finish-first pressure along the corridor is efficient. Retreat profile exists only for a concrete low-health switch (below 0.35 health ratio): it raises kiting range, tightens the fire gate and widens escape horizon. Enemy movement/attack behaviour for type 222 is unverified, so the plan is marked to replan on new_enemy_mechanism.",
